# Commit messages (Cursor Generate Commit Message + Agent)

When generating a Git commit message for this repository, ALWAYS use Conventional Commits.

Format (one short subject line, no trailing period):

```text
type(scope): summary
```

Types: feat, fix, refactor, style, docs, test, chore, perf, ci

Scope when clear: web, api, portal, auth, clinics, i18n

Examples:

```text
feat(portal): add Super Admin clinics live search
fix(auth): block letters in phone input
style(portal): match Search and Add Clinic button widths
refactor(web): extract PortalClinicsPanel
chore: tighten commit message conventions
```

Rules:

- Prefer this format even if recent `git log` messages are long essays.
- Do NOT write multi-sentence subjects like "Refactor X by doing Y, enhancing Z..."
- Subject under ~72 characters, imperative mood.
- Optional short body only when needed; never restate the diff file-by-file.
- Project has `.commitlintrc.json` extending `@commitlint/config-conventional` — messages must pass that style.
